WEBVTT

00:01.890 --> 00:03.100
Adam...

00:03.550 --> 00:05.260
I-I can't take it anymore.

00:05.260 --> 00:07.610
Yeah, of course.

00:07.610 --> 00:09.500
It's okay. Go get some sleep.

00:11.600 --> 00:13.810
Master... what is this?

00:15.030 --> 00:16.130
A child.

00:16.130 --> 00:17.410
A newborn.

00:17.410 --> 00:18.440
A baby.

00:19.980 --> 00:21.480
Erm...

00:21.480 --> 00:25.530
Anyway, we're going to have you 
support us in raising her.

00:26.560 --> 00:31.070
We can't ask anyone for help 
because of our circumstances.

00:31.760 --> 00:33.590
This is Philomela.

00:34.270 --> 00:35.380
Please.

00:39.400 --> 00:41.950
Iris and I are both sleep deprived.

00:42.510 --> 00:44.070
I'm going to catch up a bit, too.

00:58.980 --> 01:02.000
Lady Philomela.

01:39.950 --> 01:41.570
Shall we start heading back?

01:42.020 --> 01:44.080
Yes, Master.

03:38.720 --> 03:42.330
Spider of the water surface, 
spin a string of silver.

03:42.760 --> 03:46.000
Sheep of glass, weave the silver hairs.

03:46.520 --> 03:51.030
Mirror of silver, show the form of danger.

03:51.380 --> 03:54.240
Seal away the dangers that 
may befall the child.

03:56.020 --> 03:58.070
That should ease her fever.

03:58.070 --> 03:59.630
I wanna play.

03:58.930 --> 04:01.230
Let's leave some in the fridge.

04:00.170 --> 04:01.390
Not today.

04:01.230 --> 04:01.910
Yes.

04:08.780 --> 04:12.140
I haven't seen you use sorcery in a while.

04:12.520 --> 04:16.670
That was a primitive hex for 
transferring symptoms to a doll.

04:17.570 --> 04:21.010
Hexes are my favorite kind of sorcery.

04:21.550 --> 04:24.040
Though you wouldn't normally 
use them on children.

04:24.470 --> 04:28.020
Hey, you're getting better at that.

04:28.830 --> 04:33.650
Artificial fairies aren't normally thought 
to change from their original settings.

04:34.040 --> 04:35.330
Go me.

04:36.330 --> 04:39.080
Am I growing?

04:39.570 --> 04:41.230
You sure are.

04:41.230 --> 04:42.900
Everyone in this family is.

04:43.640 --> 04:46.420
You fail, you scramble to find remedies,

04:47.000 --> 04:49.670
and when you succeed, you fail again.

04:51.220 --> 04:54.580
We weren't allowed to fail 
back at my other home.

04:55.130 --> 04:57.250
Which home would that be?

04:57.250 --> 05:01.100
Ah, I haven't told you about it.

05:01.920 --> 05:05.580
The Sargants have always 
had someone to serve.

05:06.070 --> 05:08.190
We specialize in doing people's dirty work.

05:08.710 --> 05:11.870
Getting rid of people that 
our masters don't like.

05:12.390 --> 05:15.400
Torturing people for information.

05:15.930 --> 05:19.290
One day, Iris was sold off to us.

05:20.350 --> 05:22.910
As a lab rat for my sorcery.

05:25.900 --> 05:31.700
Use her to practice
 restraint so as not to kill.

05:32.950 --> 05:33.850
Yes.

05:47.880 --> 05:50.150
Hold still, damn it!

05:50.150 --> 05:55.920
I'll never, <i>ever</i> bow to you!

06:04.460 --> 06:09.830
So anyway, thanks to 
Iris, I was disciplined.

06:10.270 --> 06:15.080
The would-be heir abandoned his mother,
 his lineage, and his family name.

06:15.080 --> 06:16.630
And now he's here.

06:17.750 --> 06:19.020
Your mother...

06:20.140 --> 06:24.050
She thinks of me as
 an extension of herself.

06:24.500 --> 06:25.870
I see.

06:26.410 --> 06:27.900
By the way, Master...

06:28.870 --> 06:30.330
It's burning.

06:37.910 --> 06:39.170
Has she calmed down?

06:39.660 --> 06:40.500
Yes.

06:40.830 --> 06:44.970
It seems that the treat I'd given 
her wasn't what she wanted today.

06:44.970 --> 06:47.190
Thanks, Alcyone.

06:47.190 --> 06:48.350
I appreciate it.

06:49.760 --> 06:53.490
Master has informed me that this is 
the most important task in the world.

06:53.490 --> 06:55.840
Nothing is of a higher priority.

06:59.660 --> 07:00.760
Good girl.

07:02.190 --> 07:05.920
Man, I wish I had a camera.

07:06.930 --> 07:09.930
All the smiles, the sobbing, the silliness...

07:09.930 --> 07:12.040
It's all gone in an instant.

07:12.040 --> 07:14.110
A camera?

07:14.110 --> 07:17.460
We can't have any photos used 
against us, so we don't have one.

07:18.040 --> 07:21.150
We're on the run from
 a scary witch, after all.

07:21.580 --> 07:25.650
My parents used to take lots of photos.

07:25.650 --> 07:27.780
The walls at home were covered in them.

07:27.780 --> 07:31.670
Master said your mother sold you, too.

07:33.630 --> 07:36.260
Our financial situation
 went bad in an instant.

07:36.940 --> 07:39.900
Still, who'd have thought I'd 
end up eloping with the guy

07:39.900 --> 07:42.850
I headbutted out of 
frustration when I got sold off?

07:42.850 --> 07:46.040
Life sure is unpredictable.

07:46.040 --> 07:47.270
Frustration?

07:47.600 --> 07:51.160
He was a well-dressed kid who 
didn't have a worry in the world.

07:51.440 --> 07:55.470
And I was told he was about to experiment
 on me. Of course I was pissed.

07:58.740 --> 08:00.830
Do you hate Master?

08:04.840 --> 08:06.190
I'm not sure.

08:06.910 --> 08:10.880
But we ended up having 
this cute girl together.

08:16.290 --> 08:17.780
I'm scared, though.

08:18.400 --> 08:24.260
I don't know if I'll be able to prioritize her 
if something ever really does happen.

08:25.600 --> 08:32.120
After all, I'm the child of someone 
who sold off their own kid.

08:39.590 --> 08:40.680
My duty,

08:42.130 --> 08:49.130
even if you or Master were to do such 
a thing, is to protect Lady Philomela.

08:52.800 --> 08:58.400
Hey, Alcyone, please 
remember today, too.

08:59.090 --> 09:01.950
So if there's ever a day when neither
 Adam nor I can tell her ourselves,

09:02.370 --> 09:10.460
you'll be there to teach her about the difficult
 times and the joyful times, like today.

09:17.460 --> 09:21.980
Ham, cheese, bacon, potatoes, carrots.

09:22.750 --> 09:25.090
That should be about all 
the shopping I need to do.

09:28.650 --> 09:31.070
Well, this is rather alarming.

09:31.070 --> 09:32.220
In the city, no less.

09:32.220 --> 09:37.040
The mistress wants me to inform 
you that playtime is over.

09:38.390 --> 09:39.920
Playtime, huh?

09:40.670 --> 09:42.920
That sounds like something she'd say.

09:43.910 --> 09:45.990
<i>A barrier to keep people away.</i>

09:45.990 --> 09:49.060
Well, she hadn't sent anyone after us.

09:49.060 --> 09:51.400
I figured she was toying with us.

09:51.400 --> 09:53.760
No more playing house.

09:53.760 --> 09:56.310
With your daughter as grown as she is,

09:56.310 --> 09:58.490
we can no longer allow you to roam free.

09:58.720 --> 10:02.200
Lord Adam, we ask you 
to return to the mansion.

10:02.640 --> 10:06.590
So she was waiting for her granddaughter 
to grow old enough to use as a hostage.

10:13.010 --> 10:15.000
Shit! She's shooting at us!

10:15.930 --> 10:17.710
Open the damn door!

10:18.210 --> 10:19.750
Shoot the doorknob.

10:19.750 --> 10:21.760
We're breaking in!

10:21.760 --> 10:22.720
Master...

10:23.140 --> 10:23.890
Master.

10:23.890 --> 10:24.760
Alcyone!

10:25.140 --> 10:26.760
We'll catch up later.

10:26.760 --> 10:29.220
Don't give her to that house!

10:29.550 --> 10:31.500
No, Mom!

10:31.500 --> 10:32.770
I'm not going!

10:34.080 --> 10:35.770
Mom!

10:37.250 --> 10:39.250
Wait for us up ahead.

10:41.020 --> 10:42.040
Go!

10:42.040 --> 10:43.210
I'll be right behind you!

10:43.210 --> 10:44.390
Mom!

10:43.550 --> 10:44.420
Don't shoot!

10:44.420 --> 10:45.410
You'll hit the child!

10:54.550 --> 10:57.230
We shouldn't have lost the child.

10:57.660 --> 10:59.680
We didn't expect you to give up your life.

11:02.570 --> 11:03.780
What...

11:08.580 --> 11:13.720
Some kind of hex to mirror 
an injury to your attacker?

11:18.050 --> 11:20.450
B-But you've sacrificed yourself.

11:21.000 --> 11:22.290
And?

11:23.200 --> 11:25.520
Now that I know what 
the outside world is like...

11:25.520 --> 11:26.890
I'd never...

11:28.590 --> 11:30.190
go back to that damn place.

11:31.360 --> 11:34.740
I'm more certain of that 
than anything else.

11:35.800 --> 11:37.820
I'd rather die than go back.

11:37.820 --> 11:38.980
Stop...

11:38.980 --> 11:39.710
No!

11:42.440 --> 11:47.280
Hey, Mom. Why don't we make one last bet?

11:49.640 --> 11:53.770
Let's make sure I never see you again.

11:58.950 --> 12:02.820
My life sure is shit.

12:03.870 --> 12:09.680
You bastards. Do you know how 
long I've been with that guy?

12:10.150 --> 12:12.360
He pretends to be all nice,

12:12.360 --> 12:16.370
but he's just a cocky brat who 
can't help but try to get even.

12:22.410 --> 12:27.610
This curse won't protect you, 
but it'll take revenge.

12:29.830 --> 12:31.750
So you want me to trust you?

12:32.090 --> 12:33.260
Sorry.

12:33.260 --> 12:35.580
I'm sure you don't want to 
be hurt in the first place.

12:37.580 --> 12:39.060
I don't care.

12:39.060 --> 12:43.390
It'll help me remember my anger and 
my decision to leave this place.

12:44.710 --> 12:48.320
If you really feel guilty, you'll 
become a really good sorcerer

12:49.030 --> 12:51.320
and get me out of here someday!

13:29.810 --> 13:34.140
I didn't want to die yet.

13:38.920 --> 13:45.650
<i>Master, Lady Iris, please be assured 
that I am here for this child.</i>

13:45.650 --> 13:50.340
<i>Even if I am destroyed,
 Lady Philomela will surely...</i>

13:55.100 --> 13:58.730
Damn artificial fairy, 
making us chase you down...

14:10.320 --> 14:13.630
I was given a task.

14:22.190 --> 14:25.270
So why do I...

14:37.060 --> 14:39.830
A smart dog with a new master...

14:41.460 --> 14:44.120
You're barking up the wrong tree.

14:44.480 --> 14:45.790
Who are you?

14:46.240 --> 14:50.490
I ask of the maiden only one thing now.

14:50.930 --> 14:53.210
To bring here the golden branch.

14:53.210 --> 14:57.680
The one brimming with 
the fruit of white vigor.

14:58.610 --> 15:00.510
Golden branch?

15:01.160 --> 15:07.090
<i>What an odd voice. It's like 
honey, sweet and viscous.</i>

15:07.090 --> 15:08.830
She means mistletoe.

15:09.350 --> 15:10.670
Elias.

15:11.040 --> 15:12.510
Be strong.

15:12.510 --> 15:14.030
Don't look away.

15:14.480 --> 15:16.130
But don't look into her eyes.

15:16.560 --> 15:17.950
<i>This is bad.</i>

15:18.870 --> 15:22.930
<i>I didn't expect a god like her to 
show up now of all times.</i>

15:22.930 --> 15:24.810
You, amalgamation.

15:24.810 --> 15:26.920
Dregs of the shadows of the forest.

15:27.570 --> 15:31.090
A pile of decaying twigs and 
leaves, death and winter.

15:31.830 --> 15:34.360
Child of my domain.

15:34.360 --> 15:38.370
What scent of rot do you 
smell in your dreams,

15:38.370 --> 15:40.500
covered in countless pieces 
of flesh and skin?

15:43.300 --> 15:47.970
I apologize for the unsightly display, 
mistress of the winter and night.

15:48.320 --> 15:51.680
Surely my daughter had informed you...

15:51.680 --> 15:55.460
That in the coming year, you would 
give your fruit to the mother.

15:56.920 --> 15:57.830
Huh?

15:59.780 --> 16:02.600
There must have been a mistake.

16:04.810 --> 16:07.480
This maiden is still young.

16:08.040 --> 16:12.160
It would be difficult to provide 
the sacrifice to you here and now.

16:13.530 --> 16:16.500
I will soon come prepared.

16:17.200 --> 16:19.550
Please forgive me for now.

16:21.810 --> 16:22.960
<i>Did that not work?</i>

16:23.610 --> 16:25.970
<i>This is my only option, though.</i>

16:25.970 --> 16:27.080
I do...

16:30.360 --> 16:33.270
I do smell the coming war.

16:34.540 --> 16:39.810
Though there are neither spears, 
nor swords, nor shields, nor war horns...

16:43.110 --> 16:44.930
Indeed, indeed.

16:45.270 --> 16:50.010
While under siege, none would have 
the time to search for the fruit of love.

16:50.010 --> 16:51.280
<i>Shit...</i>

16:51.280 --> 16:53.830
<i>I don't want to deal with either of them.</i>

16:53.830 --> 16:54.860
In that case...

16:54.860 --> 16:56.780
What do you desire,

16:56.780 --> 17:03.680
little bird that will take the form of a beast
 symbolizing battle with heretics just to fly?

17:05.210 --> 17:06.240
<i>What...</i>

17:06.660 --> 17:08.440
<i>What do I want?</i>

17:08.440 --> 17:09.690
<i>What to do?</i>

17:10.440 --> 17:11.280
I—

17:11.280 --> 17:11.840
Chise.

17:12.590 --> 17:16.360
If you don't want to give up 
something precious to you,

17:16.360 --> 17:18.330
you mustn't speak a wish to a god.

17:20.670 --> 17:22.940
You clever little runt.

17:22.940 --> 17:27.360
Then I shall lend you my help for now,

17:27.980 --> 17:31.360
provided that I will be given 
the golden branch later.

17:31.360 --> 17:33.420
What? What are they talking about?

17:33.420 --> 17:35.200
What are they doing here?

17:35.560 --> 17:38.040
Seek my form.

17:38.040 --> 17:40.160
Create my outline.

17:40.160 --> 17:43.030
Bind me to myself.

17:43.030 --> 17:44.550
Speak it.

17:49.270 --> 17:55.170
Chise, neither you nor I can refuse 
the requests of an ancient god.

17:55.790 --> 18:00.040
I don't know whether this will make 
our situation better or worse, but...

18:00.040 --> 18:03.710
If I have to do it now, I'll 
do it first and then decide.

18:04.430 --> 18:06.870
That's how I've known you to be.

18:07.730 --> 18:09.190
Follow my lead.

18:10.540 --> 18:13.780
Now that you've been called, 
you should know its name.

18:17.080 --> 18:19.050
Beautiful is the battlefield.

18:19.050 --> 18:21.360
Beautiful is the blood-tainted sky.

18:21.360 --> 18:22.500
Stop the chanting!

18:22.790 --> 18:24.780
It's an atrophied god!

18:25.670 --> 18:27.900
Kill the medium before she's given her name!

18:30.600 --> 18:32.370
Why would I allow that?

18:32.730 --> 18:34.570
Sing your grief.

18:34.570 --> 18:36.500
Wash the blood away from your armor.

18:36.860 --> 18:39.610
Queen of nightmares, cackling in the night;

18:39.610 --> 18:43.360
mistress of heroes, 
mother of warriors...

18:43.860 --> 18:45.810
Bring to your head the crown of thorns.

18:46.250 --> 18:48.140
Bring here your name.

18:49.440 --> 18:52.810
Bring here the name of the goddess Morrígan.

18:57.760 --> 19:03.330
Over millennia, I lost my 
people and my language,

19:03.860 --> 19:06.010
and my land was taken from me.

19:07.270 --> 19:13.200
Millennia later, I was summoned 
by the maiden from afar.

19:14.950 --> 19:16.220
What are these things?!

19:16.570 --> 19:21.720
Now, my fine, strong men, this is
 the battle you've been waiting for.

19:22.030 --> 19:23.410
Tear them apart.

19:23.960 --> 19:28.210
Pierce their flesh, break their 
bones and cut them down.

19:28.210 --> 19:31.900
Live valiantly and steal pathetically.

19:32.320 --> 19:35.400
Flee pitifully and die in flames.

19:35.820 --> 19:45.250
Know that none who fight on the goddess 
Morrígan's battlefield will escape!

19:54.770 --> 19:57.250
Poor thing.

19:57.830 --> 20:00.910
You never expected your first 
battle to end like this, did you?

20:05.670 --> 20:09.770
It looks like we'll be able to reach the 
mansion without being attacked, thanks to her.

20:10.300 --> 20:16.280
It turned out well, but a god's 
actions really are unpredictable.

20:16.680 --> 20:18.450
As are yours.

20:18.890 --> 20:20.020
Chise?

20:20.020 --> 20:21.120
It's nothing.

20:21.120 --> 20:22.230
Let's go.

20:23.700 --> 20:25.880
<i>I didn't think I had any other choice.</i>

20:25.880 --> 20:29.110
<i>I'm just glad I don't know anyone here.</i>

20:29.500 --> 20:34.530
<i>Do I really know how to 
distinguish people from sheep?</i>

20:39.090 --> 20:40.610
A-Are we out?

20:40.610 --> 20:42.110
Where are we?

20:42.110 --> 20:44.510
The Sargant family's yard.

20:44.980 --> 20:48.780
So, what happened, anyway?

20:48.780 --> 20:50.170
A lot of stuff.

20:50.170 --> 20:51.360
You look pale.

20:52.040 --> 20:54.560
Guys, hear me out.

20:54.560 --> 20:56.390
We should get our objectives in order.

20:56.760 --> 20:57.690
Our objectives?

20:58.000 --> 20:59.790
What are we prioritizing?

20:59.790 --> 21:03.480
We need to get that straight, or we 
could end up turning on each other.

21:04.480 --> 21:07.970
Chise and I will bring Philomela back alive.

21:07.970 --> 21:08.950
All right?

21:08.950 --> 21:09.770
Yeah.

21:10.140 --> 21:11.420
Lucy?

21:11.420 --> 21:15.550
I have tons of questions 
for her and this family.

21:15.550 --> 21:16.660
Zoe?

21:16.660 --> 21:21.750
I want Lu—<i>everyone</i> to come home safe.

21:21.750 --> 21:22.890
So I'm helping.

21:23.410 --> 21:25.460
What about you, Mr. Ainsworth?

21:25.460 --> 21:28.740
Supervising to make sure my apprentice 
doesn't get in over her head.

21:28.740 --> 21:30.540
Mr. Zaccheroni? Actually, never mind.

21:30.540 --> 21:31.390
Hey!

21:32.030 --> 21:35.050
I think all our interests line up.

21:35.050 --> 21:36.700
So first, Philomela...

21:41.420 --> 21:42.560
A werewolf?!

21:43.710 --> 21:44.870
It's her!

21:44.870 --> 21:47.280
Guys, I'll see you up ahead!

21:47.280 --> 21:49.350
Zoe? Why...

21:50.390 --> 21:54.270
This job is for me.

21:54.270 --> 21:55.490
Go without me!

21:58.890 --> 22:02.050
He's right that it's the 
best way to buy time...

22:02.050 --> 22:03.100
But...

22:11.700 --> 22:13.110
Man...

22:13.110 --> 22:16.610
I was hoping I could use this 
when Lucy was in a bind, but...

22:18.310 --> 22:20.730
Things don't ever work out 
the way you want, huh?
